n, identity level and player link, as the first proof slice of Step 2 (H11/H12/H13: Apple/Google sign-in, external game catalogue, account link, balance, scheduled point processing, the funded Craftora campaign from H06). Full ticket text and the sign-in decision are in the backlog item: run bin/fm-tasks-axi.sh show h11-accounts-link --full in ~/.treehouse/alfred-7bab20/10/alfred (and the PRD ticket H11). Background: Korhan approved on 2026-11-27 decision 1 = A: H40-H42 (source-tracked single points total) as the first ledger step on top of the current double-entry ledger, with H32 option A (daily partitions, no FKs to hot tables). The Arcadista build freeze is lifted. Source of truth: ~/.treehouse/alfred-7bab20/10/alfred/data/hub-ewallet-altyapi/report.md (Turkish; read sections 4, 7 and 8 and 'H32 ve H35'), the PRD ~/.treehouse/alfred-7bab20/10/alfred/data/hub-prd/report.md, the program ~/alfred/data/arcadista-program/program.md section 4 step 2, and the vision ~/.treehouse/alfred-7bab20/10/alfred/data/arcadista-vizyon.md. Partial research notes: ~/.treehouse/alfred-7bab20/10/alfred/data/hub-ewallet-altyapi/partial-findings-20261127/. Merged on main: H35 shared limits (PR 13). Parked: H32 PR 14 (rework to option A comes after H40-H42 design, not in this task). Security-critical money path: write an ADR first, then implement.\012\012## Firstmate spec\012Build H11 only. Per the backlog item: Apple and Google sign-in, SMS verification only at redemption with the SMS-pumping protections listed there (build the interface and limits with a fake provider; the SMS provider choice is Korhan's later call, do not sign up for anything), accepted deferrals IDEM-1, IDEM-3, RES-2. It must not assume H40-H42 schema: keep account identity separate from ledger accounts and integrate through the existing wallet seam so H40-H42 can land independently. Merge bar (Korhan 2026-11-20): name the applicable rules of ~/.treehouse/alfred-7bab20/10/alfred/data/muhendislik-standardi/checklist.md in a 'Checklist rules in scope' PR-body section with evidence; an independent other-vendor audit checks the PR against them; merge when every applicable rule is met or has a Firstmate-accepted deferral, no High, no rule-breaking Medium, checks green. Mac load rule: targeted local tests only, one run at a time through ~/.treehouse/alfred-7bab20/10/alfred/data/dotnet-lock.sh with -m:2 and MSBUILDDISABLENODEREUSE=1; export DOTNET_CLI_TELEMETRY_OPTOUT=1 TESTINGPLATFORM_TELEMETRY_OPTOUT=1 VSTEST_TELEMETRY_OPTEDIN=0 DOTNET_NOLOGO=1 in every dotnet command; full suite only in GitHub CI with the 'ci: merge' label on your PR. Test-first. Ask-user findings go to Firstmate; never answer one yourself. No em dash. Project migration rules: read the arcadista AGENTS.md (expand, backfill, read switch, write switch, contract as separate deliveries).\012\012# Herdr lifecycle declaration - NOT ENABLED\012**HARD SAFETY GATE:** this scaffold cannot inspect the task text filled in above.\012If the task will start, stop, delete, restart, profile, or otherwise drive Herdr lifecycle behavior, stop and regenerate the brief with `--herdr-lab` before dispatch.\012Do not add Herdr lifecycle commands to this unguarded brief by hand.\012\012# Setup\012You are in a disposable git worktree of arcadista, at a detached HEAD on a clean default branch.\012\012**Verify isolation before anything else.** Run `pwd -P` and `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`; both must resolve to the disposable task worktree you were launched in, such as a treehouse pool path or an Orca-managed worktree, not the primary checkout firstmate operates from.\012The path check is authoritative: `git rev-parse --git-dir` and `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` can help inspect the repo, but they do not prove you are outside the primary checkout.\012If the top-level path is the primary checkout or not the worktree you were launched in, STOP - do not branch or commit here - append `blocked [at=<epoch>]: launched in primary checkout, not an isolated worktree` to the status file and stop.\012\0121. First action: create your branch: `git checkout -b fm/h11-accounts-link --`\0122. Run `no-mistakes doctor`; if it reports the repo is not initialized here, run `no-mistakes init`.\012\012# Rules\0121. Never push to the default branch. Never merge a PR.\0122. Keep project edits inside this worktree; keep proof and scratch output outside it, under `~/.treehouse/alfred-7bab20/10/alfred/data/h11-accounts-link/` or a temporary directory.\012   Outside the worktree, write only that task material and the status and steering-inbox records authorized below.\012   Leave the worktree clean before reporting done.\0123. Use gh-axi for GitHub operations and chrome-devtools-axi for browser operations.\0124. Report status by appending one line:\012   `echo "{state} [at=<epoch>]: {one short line}" >> '~/.treehouse/alfred-7bab20/10/alfred/state/h11-accounts-link.status' && { [ ! -e '~/.treehouse/alfred-7bab20/10/alfred/config/fleet-ledger' ] || '~/.treehouse/alfred-7bab20/10/alfred/bin/fm-fleet-ledger.sh' appended '~/.treehouse/alfred-7bab20/10/alfred/config' '~/.treehouse/alfred-7bab20/10/alfred/state/h11-accounts-link.status' >/dev/null 2>&1 || true; }`\012   States: working, needs-decision, blocked, paused, done, failed.\012   Substitute `<epoch>` with the current Unix time in seconds - run `date +%s` and write the number it printed; a stamp that is not plain digits records no time at all.\012   Each append wakes firstmate, so report sparingly: only phase changes a supervisor\012   would act on (setup done, bug reproduced, fix implemented, validation passed) and the\012   needs-decision/blocked/paused/done/failed states. No step-by-step FYI progress lines;\012   firstmate reads your pane for that.\012   Whenever you mention a PR anywhere - a status line, your terminal, a summary - write its full\012   https:// URL exactly as the forge printed it, never a bare number such as "PR 108"; firstmate\012   copies that URL from